        "original_id": "71c9ae2a-16a8-5cdf-bffa-861d5cbba5fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andrey Zvyagintsev, Marvin Heemeyer, Mikhail Krichman\n- Works: Leviathan, The Return, The Banishment, Elena\n- Places: United States, Russia, Granby, Colorado\n- Concepts: Naboth's Vineyard, film inspiration, cinematography\n\nFacts:\n- On June 4, 2004, Marvin Heemeyer drove an armored bulldozer through Granby, Colorado, damaging 13 buildings and causing about $7 million in damage.\n- Mikhail Krichman photographed all of Andrey Zvyagintsev's films, including The Return (2003), The Banishment (2007), Elena (2010), and Leviathan (2014).\n- Andrey Zvyagintsev said that the story of Marvin Heemeyer in the United States inspired Leviathan and that he adapted it to a Russian setting.\n- Critics compared Leviathan to the biblical story of Naboth's Vineyard, in which a king seeks a subject's land and is urged by his queen to obtain it slyly.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
